  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Management of Natural Resources for Food Security of Gemela Mayan Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMKADES will train 70 indigenous Kaqchikel families in Chimaltenango in animal husbandry and will give them the calves produced by its &quot;bank&quot; of 35 cows. Its goal is to address chronic malnutrition and to enable the families to earn additional income. (GT-302)</narrative>
  </description>
